6. Documentation & Notation Specification
------------------------------------------

Documentation describing the TKA notation system (the alphabet,
letter types, position theory, orientation rules) is licensed under
Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0).
See licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt for the full text.

This ensures the notation system itself remains an open standard that
anyone can teach, reference, and build upon, while requiring attribution
to Austen Cloud and TKA.


7. Post-Mortem Open Source Provision
--------------------------------------

It is the express intent of the sole copyright holder, Austen Cloud,
that upon his death or permanent incapacitation:

  (a) ALL code in this repository currently licensed under the Elastic
      License 2.0 (Sections 3 and 4 above) shall be automatically
      relicensed under the MIT License (licenses/MIT.txt).

  (b) ALL proprietary datasets (Section 5b above) shall be released
      under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
      International License (licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt).

  (c) Components already under MIT or CC BY-SA 4.0 remain unchanged.

The purpose of this provision is to ensure that The Kinetic Alphabet
and all associated tools, knowledge, and data become freely available
to the global flow arts community and the public at large, in
perpetuity, should the original author no longer be able to steward
them. This reflects the author's belief that closing a project behind
a locked door after death is antithetical to the open-source ethos.

7.1 Definition of Triggering Event
-----------------------------------

"Death" means the legal death of the author as established by a death
certificate or equivalent official record.

"Permanent incapacitation" means any of the following:

  (i)   A court of competent jurisdiction finds the author legally
        incapacitated or appoints a guardian or conservator over his
        person or estate;
  (ii)  Two licensed physicians independently certify in writing that
        the author is permanently unable to manage his affairs; OR
  (iii) A period of 180 consecutive days during which BOTH of the
        following are true: the author is unreachable at
        austencloud@gmail.com, AND the author has made no commits or
        other public activity under the github.com/austencloud account.

Any of the three conditions above is sufficient, independently, to
establish permanent incapacitation for purposes of this provision.

7.2 Scope of Affected Repositories
------------------------------------

This provision applies to:

  - This repository (github.com/austencloud/tka-platform)
  - Any repository owned by github.com/austencloud that is tagged with
    the GitHub topic `tka`
  - Any repository explicitly listed in a file named
    POST_MORTEM_REPOS.txt at the root of this repository (if such a
    file exists at the time of the triggering event)

Personal repositories, experiments, and unrelated projects under
github.com/austencloud are NOT included unless they satisfy one of the
conditions above.

7.3 Executor and Community Fallback
-------------------------------------

Primary Executor: To be named in the author's estate planning
documents. Until such designation is recorded and publicly announced,
the primary executor position is unfilled and the community fallback
mechanism (below) is the sole path to activation.

Upon a triggering event, the primary executor (if named) is authorized
and instructed to:

  1. Verify the triggering event per Section 7.1
  2. Update all LICENSE files in repositories within scope (per
     Section 7.2) to reflect the relicensing described in (a), (b),
     and (c) above
  3. Publish a public announcement to the flow arts community
  4. Ensure continued public access to the affected repositories

Community Fallback: If no primary executor has acted within twelve
(12) months of a verified triggering event — or if no primary
executor has ever been named — any individual may initiate the
relicensing by:

  1. Opening a public GitHub issue in this repository titled
     "Post-Mortem Provision Activation" and presenting evidence of the
     triggering event (e.g., death certificate, court order, physician
     letters, or documentation of the 180-day unreachable period);
  2. Waiting a minimum of ninety (90) days for public comment and
     objection on that issue;
  3. If no credible objection is raised, submitting a pull request
     that updates the LICENSE files in all repositories within scope
     per Section 7.2.

This community fallback exists to ensure the provision cannot be
silently ignored. It reflects the author's intent that the work
become freely available even if no designated person remains to act.

7.4 Reversibility
-------------------

This provision is a declaration of present intent and may be modified
or revoked by the author at any time prior to a triggering event by
committing a change to this LICENSE file under the author's own
GitHub authorship. After a triggering event, this provision is
irrevocable.

7.5 Estate Planning Note
--------------------------

This declaration is intended to be supplemented by, but does not
require, corresponding instructions in the author's estate planning
documents. The community fallback mechanism in Section 7.3 ensures
the provision is self-executing even in the absence of such documents
or a named executor.

If you believe this provision has been triggered and the repository
has not yet been relicensed, open a public GitHub issue as described
in the Community Fallback mechanism above.


